# Bun Cha Bowl

Based on [https://www.recipetineats.com/bun-cha-vietnamese-meatballs/](https://www.recipetineats.com/bun-cha-vietnamese-meatballs) ([wayback](http://web.archive.org/web/20251228043945/https://www.recipetineats.com/bun-cha-vietnamese-meatballs/)), [https://www.budgetbytes.com/bun-cha/](https://www.budgetbytes.com/bun-cha/), and [Lazy Cat Kitchen - Vegan Bun Noodles Tofu](https://www.lazycatkitchen.com/vegan-bun-noodles-tofu) ([wayback](http://web.archive.org/web/20251205031423/https://www.lazycatkitchen.com/vegan-bun-noodles-tofu/))

{ rating="0" image="None" }
:::
:::

## Ingredients

### For Meatballs (Pork, Chicken, or Turkey)

- [ ] 1.5 lbs [ground pork]{ ing="ground-pork" }, chicken, or turkey
- [ ] 3 cloves [garlic]{ ing="garlic" }, minced
- [ ] 2 stalks [lemongrass]{ ing="lemongrass" }, tender white parts only, finely minced (or 2 tsp lemongrass paste, or 1 tsp lime zest + 1 tsp grated ginger)
- [ ] 2 [shallots]{ ing="shallots" }, finely minced
- [ ] 2 Tbsp [fish sauce]{ ing="fish-sauce" }
- [ ] 1 Tbsp [brown sugar]{ ing="brown-sugar" }
- [ ] 1 Tbsp [neutral oil]{ ing="neutral-oil" }
- [ ] 1 tsp [black pepper]{ ing="black-pepper" }
- [ ] 1/4 tsp [salt]{ ing="salt" }

### For Tofu (Alternative to Meatballs)

- [ ] 2 (14-ounce) blocks [extra-firm tofu]{ ing="extra-firm-tofu" }, pressed and cubed
- [ ] 2 Tbsp [cornstarch]{ ing="cornstarch" } (for extra crispy coating)

#### Tofu Marinade (also serves as dressing)

- [ ] 6 Tbsp [tamari or soy sauce]{ ing="tamari-or-soy-sauce" }
- [ ] 2-3 tsp [sambal oelek]{ ing="sambal-oelek" }, adjust to taste
- [ ] 4 Tbsp (1/4 cup) fresh [lime juice]{ ing="lime-juice" }
- [ ] 4 tsp [maple syrup]{ ing="maple-syrup" }
- [ ] 1 small [garlic clove]{ ing="garlic-clove" }, finely grated or minced
- [ ] 2 tsp [finely grated ginger]{ ing="finely-grated-ginger" }
- [ ] 2 tsp [toasted sesame oil]{ ing="toasted-sesame-oil" }

### Nuoc Cham Dipping Sauce

- [ ] 1/4 cup [fish sauce]{ ing="fish-sauce" } (or soy sauce for vegetarian)
- [ ] 1/4 cup [lime juice]{ ing="lime-juice" } (about 2-3 limes)
- [ ] 1/4 cup [water]{ ing="water" }
- [ ] 3 Tbsp [sugar]{ ing="sugar" }
- [ ] 2 cloves [garlic]{ ing="garlic" }, minced
- [ ] 1-2 [Thai chili peppers]{ ing="thai-chili-peppers" }, thinly sliced (or 1 tsp chili garlic sauce)
- [ ] 2 Tbsp [rice vinegar]{ ing="rice-vinegar" }

### Rice Base

- [ ] 2 cups [rice vermicelli noodles]{ ing="rice-vermicelli-noodles" }, long-grain brown jasmine rice (healthiest), or white rice
- [ ] 3 cups [water]{ ing="water" }

### Quick Pickled Vegetables (Do Chua)

- [ ] 1 large [carrot]{ ing="carrot" }, julienned or shredded
- [ ] 1/2 [daikon radish]{ ing="daikon-radish" }, julienned (or substitute with extra carrot)
- [ ] 1/4 cup [rice vinegar]{ ing="rice-vinegar" }
- [ ] 1/4 cup [water]{ ing="water" }
- [ ] 2 Tbsp [sugar]{ ing="sugar" }
- [ ] 1/2 tsp [salt]{ ing="salt" }

### Bowl Toppings

- [ ] 4 cups [mixed greens]{ ing="mixed-greens" } (lettuce, butter lettuce, or herbs like mint, cilantro, Thai basil)
- [ ] 1 [cucumber]{ ing="cucumber" }, thinly sliced
- [ ] 1/2 cup [crushed roasted peanuts]{ ing="crushed-roasted-peanuts" }
- [ ] 3 [green onions]{ ing="green-onions" }, thinly sliced
- [ ] Fresh [mint and cilantro leaves]{ ing="mint-and-cilantro-leaves" }
- [ ] [Lime wedges]{ ing="lime-wedges" }
- [ ] 8 oz [oyster mushrooms]{ ing="oyster-mushrooms" }, torn into strips (optional, can be sautéed or added raw)
- [ ] 1/2 head [red cabbage]{ ing="red-cabbage" }, thinly sliced (optional, can be stir-fried or added raw)

## Recipe

### Make the Quick Pickles

1. In a medium bowl, combine [rice vinegar]{ ing="rice-vinegar" }, [water]{ ing="water" }, [sugar]{ ing="brown-sugar" }, and [salt]{ ing="salt" }. Stir until [sugar]{ ing="sugar" } dissolves
1. Add julienned [carrot]{ ing="carrot" } and daikon. Let sit for at least 30 minutes (can be made up to 2 weeks ahead)

### Prepare the Nuoc Cham Sauce

1. In a bowl, combine [fish sauce]{ ing="fish-sauce" }, [lime juice]{ ing="lime-juice" }, [water]{ ing="water" }, and [sugar]{ ing="brown-sugar" }. Stir until [sugar]{ ing="sugar" } dissolves
1. Add minced [garlic]{ ing="garlic" }, [chili peppers]{ ing="thai-chili-peppers" }, and [rice vinegar]{ ing="rice-vinegar" }. Set aside (flavors improve as it sits)

### Cook the Rice

1. Rinse brown rice under cold [water]{ ing="water" } until water runs clear
1. Combine rice and [water]{ ing="water" } in a pot or rice cooker. Bring to a boil, reduce heat to low, cover, and simmer for 40-45 minutes until tender
1. Remove from heat and let sit covered for 10 minutes, then fluff with a fork

### Make the Meatballs

1. In a large bowl, combine ground meat with [garlic]{ ing="garlic" }, [lemongrass]{ ing="lemongrass" }, [shallots]{ ing="shallots" }, [fish sauce]{ ing="fish-sauce" }, [brown sugar]{ ing="brown-sugar" }, [oil]{ ing="neutral-oil" }, [black pepper]{ ing="black-pepper" }, and [salt]{ ing="salt" }
1. Mix gently until just combined (don’t overmix). Form into small meatballs (~1.5 inches) or flatten into small patties
1. Cooking options:

   - Air fry: 375F for 12-15 minutes, flipping halfway, until golden and cooked through (internal temp 165F)
   - Pan fry: Heat 1 Tbsp oil in a large skillet over medium heat. Cook meatballs/patties 3-4 minutes per side until golden and cooked through
   - Broil: Place on a foil-lined baking sheet. Broil 4-5 inches from heat for 5-6 minutes per side

### Prepare the Tofu (Alternative Method)

1. Press [tofu]{ ing="extra-firm-tofu" } for at least 30 minutes, then cut into 1-inch cubes
1. Make marinade: In a bowl, whisk together tamari, [sambal oelek]{ ing="sambal-oelek" }, [lime juice]{ ing="lime-juice" }, [maple syrup]{ ing="maple-syrup" }, [garlic]{ ing="garlic" }, [ginger]{ ing="finely-grated-ginger" }, and [sesame oil]{ ing="toasted-sesame-oil" }
1. Reserve 3/4 of the marinade in a separate container for later use as dressing
1. Pour remaining 1/4 of marinade over [tofu]{ ing="extra-firm-tofu" } cubes in a shallow container. Marinate for minimum 30 minutes or up to overnight, occasionally spooning marinade over exposed cubes
1. After marinating, remove [tofu]{ ing="extra-firm-tofu" } from marinade and pat dry. Toss with [cornstarch]{ ing="cornstarch" } until evenly coated for extra crispiness
1. Cooking options:

   - Bake: Heat oven to 400F. Arrange cornstarch-coated tofu on parchment-lined baking sheet. Bake 25-30 minutes, flipping halfway, until golden and crispy
   - Air fry: 375F for 15-18 minutes, shaking basket halfway through
   - Pan fry: Heat 1 Tbsp oil in skillet over medium-high heat. Cook tofu cubes 3-4 minutes per side until golden on all sides

### Assemble Bowls

1. Start with a base of brown rice in each bowl
1. Add a handful of [mixed greens]{ ing="mixed-greens" }, [cucumber]{ ing="cucumber" } slices, and pickled vegetables
1. Top with meatballs or [tofu]{ ing="extra-firm-tofu" } cubes
1. Garnish with crushed [peanuts]{ ing="crushed-roasted-peanuts" }, [green onions]{ ing="green-onions" }, fresh mint, and cilantro
1. For meat version: Serve with nuoc cham [sauce]{ ing="fish-sauce" } on the side or drizzled over the bowl
1. For [tofu]{ ing="extra-firm-tofu" } version: Drizzle with reserved tofu marinade/dressing (the 3/4 you set aside)
1. Serve with [lime wedges]{ ing="lime-wedges" }

## Notes

- **Lemongrass substitute:** Use lemongrass paste (2 tsp per stalk) or 1 Tbsp lemon zest + 1 tsp grated ginger per stalk
- **Sambal oelek substitute:** Equal amount sriracha, or 1/2 tsp red pepper flakes + 1/2 tsp rice vinegar per 1 tsp sambal
- **Dark soy sauce substitute:** Regular soy sauce + 1/4 tsp molasses or brown sugar per 1 Tbsp dark soy
- **Thai chili substitute:** Serrano peppers, or 1/2 tsp red pepper flakes per chili
- **Daikon substitute:** Use all carrots for the pickles, or add thinly sliced radishes
- **Cornstarch coating:** The cornstarch coating on tofu creates extra crispiness. Pat tofu dry after marinating before tossing with cornstarch
- **Tofu marinade efficiency:** The Lazy Cat Kitchen method uses one marinade for both marinating and dressing, saving time and reducing waste
- **Oyster mushrooms:** Tear along natural grain for better texture. Can substitute shiitake or button mushrooms. Sauté in oil until browned (4-5 minutes) or add raw for crunch
- **Red cabbage variation:** For a cooked cabbage option, stir-fry sliced red cabbage with soy sauce and rice vinegar for 5-7 minutes until softened but still crunchy. Adds color and nutrients
- **Make ahead:** Pickles last 2 weeks. Nuoc cham sauce lasts 1 week. Tofu marinade/dressing lasts 1 week. Meatballs can be shaped and frozen raw, or cooked and refrigerated for 3-4 days. Marinated tofu can be cooked and refrigerated for 4-5 days
- **Meal prep:** This bowl reheats well. Store components separately and assemble when ready to eat. For tofu version, store reserved marinade separately and drizzle when serving
